<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonka II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonka II was a ruler of the Velanati Chodas, a dynasty of chiefs in coastal Andhra. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a> region weakened in the 12th century, he ruled much of the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Godavari rivers from Chandavolu, nominally under the Chola emperors but in practice independently.</p></div>
